al exposure for personal conviction, and it flattens the real diversity in Lebanon. That doesn't mean religion isn't important in Lebanon. It just means the group is too varied to label that way with any practical reliability. I know that might not be the answer you wanted, but I hope it clarifies where I stand. If you still feel differently, I'm not going to argue you into changing your personal belief—but I would gently suggest that your new hire might not share it, and the safest, kindest thing you can do is let her show you who she is.
